# Copy this to .env.local (already gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Never commit a real API key to this file — it's a public repo.

# Optional third-tier RPC fallback (Ethereum, Base, BNB Chain, Arbitrum,
# Avalanche, Abstract, HyperEVM, Plasma, Stable) — see src/wagmi.js and
# src/solanaRpc.js. Every chain already has two free, no-key RPC tiers
# without this; setting it just adds a third, paid-provider layer.
VITE_ALCHEMY_API_KEY=

# Server-only (no VITE_ prefix — never bundled into the client, never
# shipped inside the mobile app either, since mobile calls the SAME
# api/v1/bridge/fallback-quote.js proxy rather than holding its own
# copy). Powers the second-source Swap fallback (api/v1/bridge/
# fallback-quote.js) tried only when Relay itself has no route at any
# fee — same-chain Swap only. Omitting either key just disables that
# one provider (a clear "isn't configured yet" error, not a crash);
# both are optional, independent of each other.
# Get a key: https://portal.1inch.dev
ONEINCH_API_KEY=
# Get a key: https://0x.org (Swap API v2 — dashboard.0x.org)
ZEROX_API_KEY=
# OKX DEX Aggregator — needs all three or none (same "isn't configured
# yet" fallback as above). Get credentials: https://web3.okx.com/build
# (Onchain OS Dev portal → create a project → API keys). Requests are
# HMAC-SHA256 signed with the secret key (OKX's own platform-wide
# signing convention), never sent anywhere themselves.
OKX_API_KEY=
OKX_SECRET_KEY=
OKX_PASSPHRASE=

# Server-only. Salts the Vercel Blob path api/txHistoryStore.js uses to
# back up mobile's own per-address transaction history (survives an
# app reinstall) — an HMAC-SHA256 secret, not a real "key" for any
# external service, so any long random string works. Generate one
# with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Missing this fails history sync closed (a clear "isn't configured
# yet" error) rather than falling back to a guessable, unsalted path.
HISTORY_SALT=

# Server-only. NEAR Intents 1Click proxy (api/v1/near/v0/*).
# NEAR_FEE_ACCOUNT: the Mango-controlled NEAR Intents account that
# receives the 0.5% app fee on NEAR routes — a 64-hex implicit account,
# a named account (e.g. fees.mango.near), or a lowercase 0x address.
# While it's empty, the quote endpoint refuses to quote at all rather
# than quoting without Mango's fee. Must match the account compiled into
# the apps (mango-pro ONE_CLICK_FEE_ACCOUNT), or their quote check
# refuses every quote.
NEAR_FEE_ACCOUNT=
# Optional 1Click partner JWT, issued through NEAR Intents' partner program.
# Without it 1Click adds its own fee on top of Mango's; with it, 1Click
# takes its share out of Mango's app fee instead.
ONE_CLICK_JWT=
